Another way to think about it is that if one-third go to swim and another one-third go to eat, then 1/3 + 1/3 = 2/3 of the penguins have left. Therefore, the remaining penguins are 1 - 2/3 = 1/3 of the original number. So 1/3 of 36 is 12. That's another way to get the same answer. So both methods agree. Therefore, confident that the answer is 12.
